{"seq":2,"slug":"interface-patterns","title":"界面模式","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/design-thinking/interaction-design/interface-patterns","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"navigation-ia","title":"导航与信息架构","url":"/l-doc-books/h/design-thinking/interaction-design/interface-patterns/navigation-ia","wordCount":3071,"readingTime":13},{"seq":2,"slug":"forms-input","title":"表单与输入设计","url":"/l-doc-books/h/design-thinking/interaction-design/interface-patterns/forms-input","wordCount":2939,"readingTime":12},{"seq":3,"slug":"states-transitions","title":"状态与过渡","url":"/l-doc-books/h/design-thinking/interaction-design/interface-patterns/states-transitions","wordCount":3642,"readingTime":15}],"introMarkdown":"# 界面模式\n\n本章聚焦数字产品中最常见的三类交互场景：用户如何找到内容（导航与信息架构）、如何输入信息（表单与输入设计）、以及界面元素如何随条件变化（状态与过渡）。这些模式不是死板的规则，而是经过数十年实践验证的解决方案库。阅读时建议结合自己正在设计的产品思考：你的导航结构是否匹配用户的心智模型？表单是否在与用户进行高效对话？状态设计是否覆盖了所有真实使用场景？\n"}